### 📚 Description

This adds an `addons` option to the `createUseFetch` / `createUseAsyncData` factories.

Addons extend the functionality of `useAsyncData` and `useFetch` in user land.
They can declare custom call-site options, mutate the merged options, wrap the handler with `middleware`, extend the composable's return value, and add additional logic through watchers, for example. They are also meant to be reusable for multiple custom instances.

This should resolve a lot of user-specific requests for new features to `useAsyncData` and `useFetch`, while keeping the core composables unopinionated.

An example of an addon:

```ts
const refreshOnFocus = defineUseFetchAddon({
  // augment the call-site options for the custom useFetch instance 👇
  setup: (options: UseFetchAddonOptions<{ refreshOnFocus?: boolean }>) => {
    // 👈 run code *before* calling `useAsyncData` in `useFetch` internally

    if (import.meta.server) { return }

    return (asyncData) => {
      // 👈 run code *after* calling `useAsyncData` in `useFetch` internally

      const focused = useWindowFocus()
      watch(focused, f => f && options.refreshOnFocus && asyncData.refresh())

      // 👇 add new properties returned from the custom `useFetch`, or override existing ones

